from fast_reference_helpers import *
P='src-b95-'
rows=[
 ('fleet','From Waste to Renewal: Circular Economy and the Ethics of Degrowth in Record of a Spaceborn Few','Vanesa Roldán-Romero, ES Review 46, indexed reproduction','https://www.scribd.com/document/954034210/esreview-46-212-242-1','indexed_scholarly_abstract','The Fleet organizes a circular resource economy around communal labor and nonhierarchical institutions.','Abstract and bounded labor-context passages only; no claim that all recycling or life support eliminates essential human work.'),
 ('engine','Engine Summer contemporary review','Destinies February 1980 indexed review; byline not checked','https://s3.us-west-1.wasabisys.com/luminist/SF/DES_1980_02.pdf','indexed_review','Little Belaire and machine remnants shape a post-technological setting.','Short indexed review, not a complete magazine or novel read; ordinary resource access is unspecified.'),
 ('mizora','Mizora','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mizora','secondary_plot_reference','Chemical food and advanced technology support the all-female society, whose eugenic/racial exclusion is explicit.','The admitted resident scope cannot be extended to all humans, men or excluded racial groups.'),
 ('automata','Automata, Mizora example','The Encyclopedia of Science Fiction editors','https://sf-encyclopedia.com/entry/automata','specialist_reference','Mizora specifically uses automata to perform domestic work.','Only the named example supports this society; broad statements about all utopias are not copied as its institutions.'),
 ('mizora-criticism','The Problematic Emancipatory Hope of the New Science in Lane’s Mizora','The Haphazard Writer’s Journal contributor','https://thehaphazardauthor.home.blog/2019/04/13/the-problematic-emancipatory-hope-of-the-new-science-in-lanes-mizora%EF%BB%BF/','labeled_critical_essay','Absence of poverty is tied to a technologically advanced state with coercive homogeneity and eugenics.','The critic’s speculation about exact executions/sterilizations is not adopted as established plot fact.'),
 ('nowhere-primary','News from Nowhere, Chapter XXVII','William Morris','https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/News_from_Nowhere/Chapter_XXVII','bounded_primary_chapter_passage','Machines could do almost all necessary work, but people increasingly choose handicraft instead.','Only the direct technological-choice exchange, not a full novel reading.'),
 ('nowhere','News from Nowhere','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/News_from_Nowhere','secondary_setting_reference','Common productive ownership, democratic control, no money/private property and pleasurable useful labor define the commonwealth.','No measured all-person work participation; enjoyable activity remains work.'),
 ('republic','The Republic of the Future','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Republic_of_the_Future','secondary_plot_reference','Socialist City has standardized homes, short workdays, automatic domestic devices and nutrition pills.','Anti-utopian aristocratic narrator and author’s satire are not neutral judgments; two-hour days are not nonworking percentages.'),
 ('foodwork','Foodwork: Racialised, gendered and classed labours','Futures of Work contributors','https://futuresofwork.co.uk/2019/12/09/foodwork-racialised-gendered-and-class-labours/','scholarly_public_commentary','Dodd’s manufactured meals arrive through pneumatic tubes, displacing household food preparation.','This fictional mechanism is distinguished from the article’s real-world agricultural-labor analysis.'),
 ('economic-sf','Economic Science Fictions lecture discussion','Caroline Edwards','https://www.drcarolineedwards.com/2018/11/26/economic-science-fictions/','scholarly_public_essay','Named early utopias use automation for leisure; Dodd’s American future is mechanized.','General literary framing does not supply each novel’s detailed ownership or household guarantees.'),
 ('griffith','Three Hundred Years Hence','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Three_Hundred_Years_Hence','secondary_bibliographic_reference','Mary Griffith’s protagonist visits improved future mid-Atlantic states.','The later William Delisle Hay book of the same title is not substituted; specific material access remains missing.'),
 ('fuller','Fuller, Alvarado M','The Encyclopedia of Science Fiction editors','https://sf-encyclopedia.com/entry/fuller_alvarado_m','specialist_author_reference','A.D. 2000 wakes a preserved protagonist in the year-2000 utopian culture.','A utopian label and future transit are not a verified automated distribution system.'),
 ('lastmen','Last and First Men','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Last_and_First_Men','secondary_future_history_reference','Different human species and the Fifth Men’s advanced technology have separate histories.','No uniform labor-independent floor across eighteen human species is inferred.'),
 ('lastmen-passage','Last and First Men, last-human-species introduction','Olaf Stapledon via 26reads','https://www.26reads.com/library/92731-last-and-first-men/17/1','indexed_primary_passage','Automatic mining, food factories and human cultivation coexist.','Short indexed introduction only; automatic sectors do not establish the whole population’s distribution institutions.'),
 ('starmaker','Star Maker, symbiotic-race passage','Olaf Stapledon via Project Gutenberg Australia','https://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks06/0601841h.html','indexed_primary_passage','Arachnid and fishlike partners develop complementary technology and perform useful intellectual/manual work.','The named symbiotic passage only; biological symbiosis and industrial achievement are not automatic necessities access.'),
 ('automation','Automation, early mechanical-system examples','The Encyclopedia of Science Fiction editors','https://sf-encyclopedia.com/entry/automation','specialist_reference','Manning’s Mech-Men, Russell’s Mechanistria and Lord Prime’s Jonnemacher novel are named in the automation tradition.','Genre placement alone does not establish a human provision population, actual floor or full plotted chronology.'),
 ('mechanistria','Vacation in the Golden Age, January 1942: Mechanistria','Jamie Todd Rubin','https://jamierubin.net/2012/01/22/vacation-in-the-golden-age-episode-31-january-1942/','secondary_story_review','A machine ecology dissects organic visitors; its machines have limited thought.','A visit under threat is not an established robot-provided human society.')
]
S=cited_sources(P,rows)
nw='No all-person useful-work census; domestic care, art, research and chosen productive activity remain work.'
refs=[P+'mizora',P+'automata',P+'mizora-criticism']
R=[scoped_record('c0835','mizora-technological-resident-order','Mizora — The technological women’s commonwealth','Mizora','The admitted female resident population supported by automata and chemical production',['book'],
 'Mary E. Bradley Lane’s Mizora','The established society visited by Vera before her return home','Living admitted Mizoran women and daughters',
 ['Men or excluded racial groups as equal beneficiaries','Historical elimination as a measured present population','The critic’s speculative exact punishment methods as canon'],
 'Mizora combines automata performing domestic work, advanced chemical food production and an order described as free from poverty. This provides a real technological reduction of necessary labor within the admitted resident population. Guarantees are provisionally favorable for those residents, with a wide interval because universal prosperity is presented through a highly exclusionary vision. The novel’s eugenics, racial hierarchy and removal of men remain explicit boundaries, not erased by the word utopia.\n\nThe surviving women direct the technology, but the short references do not establish how equally productive assets or ultimate decisions are controlled. Control therefore remains unresolved rather than equating a commonwealth label with distributed ownership or inventing an AI ruler. The state’s coercive control of bodies and belonging is distinct from routine machine operation. Chemical food and domestic automation also do not remove scholarship, care, art or other useful human activities. No all-person participation census is available, so nonworking remains null. The point concerns the functioning resident order and does not turn excluded or eliminated people into nonworkers receiving its benefits.',
 [-.5,None,None],[[-.9,.5],None,None],
 ['The references specifically combine domestic automata, chemically produced food and absence of poverty for the admitted resident population, with severe exclusion.','Human women control the technological society, but equal effective productive ownership is not established by the gathered passages.',nw],refs,1,alternatives=[2])]
refs=[P+'nowhere-primary',P+'nowhere']
R.append(scoped_record('c0836','news-nowhere-chosen-handicraft','News from Nowhere — The chosen handicraft commonwealth','News from Nowhere','Commonly owned production retaining pleasurable human labor despite machine capacity',['book'],
 'William Morris’s future commonwealth','Established post-Great Change handicraft period','Living human residents of the commonwealth',
 ['Pleasurable useful work as nonwork','Machine rejection as lack of technical capacity','The retained labor as a modern paid-job protection program'],
 'The commonwealth deliberately returns to handicraft after machines have become capable of performing almost all necessary work. Chapter XXVII says this directly: retained handwork is a preference rather than material necessity. This makes the society a particularly clear zero variant. Its reason is the pursuit of pleasurable, creative labor and equality, not an attempt to preserve conventional wage employment. Useful making remains part of ordinary life.\n\nCommon ownership and democratic control of productive resources place control toward the distributed human end. Goods are not allocated through private money or a class hierarchy, supporting strong guarantees within the shared order, though the references do not provide a comprehensive enforceable necessities charter. Voluntary and enjoyable work still counts as work, so the disappearance of wages cannot provide a nonworking percentage. The record covers the established handicraft period; earlier machine-intensive transition phases are not counted again without a separate economic assessment. Its zero label describes a realized choice among productive possibilities rather than technological backwardness.',
 [-.75,.85,None],[[-.95,-.1],[.6,1],None],
 ['The primary exchange states that machines could perform almost all necessary work but are increasingly abandoned for handicraft; common provision qualifies the strong guarantee estimate.','Common productive ownership and democratic control are explicit in the setting reference.',nw],refs,2,zero=True,locator='Chapter XXVII, Henry Morsom’s exchange on machinery and the new handicraft period'))
refs=[P+'republic',P+'foodwork',P+'economic-sf']
R.append(scoped_record('c0837','republic-future-socialist-city','The Republic of the Future — New York Socialist City','The Republic of the Future','Mechanized collective domestic provision in Dodd’s satirical future',['book'],
 'Anna Bowman Dodd’s original epistolary novella','The New York Socialist City visited in 2050','Living human inhabitants of Socialist City',
 ['The Swedish visitor’s capitalist home','Two-hour days as proof everyone is nonworking','Authorial disdain as independent evidence that material provision fails'],
 'Socialist City provides a standardized technological living environment in which manufactured nutrition is delivered to homes through tubes and automatic devices handle domestic tasks. Residents still work short days, but centralized mechanization supplies much of ordinary life and sharply reduces necessary household labor. Guarantees receive a qualified favorable estimate for that collective provision; plainness and lack of variety are not the same as absence of food or housing.\n\nEffective control is near concentrated human public authority. Uniform consumption and nominal socialism do not establish each resident’s equal ability to govern the productive system, while automatic lifts and bedmaking devices are not sovereign AI. The narrator and author treat this future satirically, so their dislike is distinguished from the depicted technical arrangement. Real work remains, including the reported two-hour daily contribution. Hours worked are not the share of people who work at all, and useful care or creative activity cannot be ignored. Nonworking therefore stays unresolved rather than being calculated from a shortened workday.',
 [-.5,.1,None],[[-.85,.25],[0,.4],None],
 ['Specific manufactured-food delivery, standardized homes and mechanized services establish collective technological support despite continuing short workdays.','Public collective administration is visible, but individual democratic control of production is not established.',nw],refs,1))

cases=[
 ('c0833','needs_evidence','fleet','The Fleet’s circular commons retains essential communal labor without a clearly verified post-work automation link.','Resource sharing and nonhierarchical institutions are not by themselves labor replacement; do not infer leisure from a closed-loop habitat.'),
 ('c0834','needs_evidence','engine','Little Belaire’s inherited machines do not establish ordinary automatic resource access in the short review.','Post-technological life and a recorded narrator are not a uniform provision society.'),
 ('c0838','needs_evidence','griffith','The improved future’s specific automated allocation mechanism remains unclear.','Scholarly grouping with automation utopias supplies a lead, not a whole necessities constitution.'),
 ('c0839','needs_evidence','fuller','A.D. 2000’s utopian culture is not accompanied by verified ordinary automatic provision.','A sleeper and futuristic transit alone do not qualify the society.'),
 ('c0840','needs_evidence','lastmen-passage','The broad human-species sequence lacks a sufficiently identified work-independent allocation order.','Automatic sectors coexist with visible human cultivation; no eighteen-species average or immortality-based leisure is invented.'),
 ('c0841','needs_evidence','starmaker','The symbiotic race’s industry and complementary biology do not establish ordinary post-work material access.','Both partners perform real useful labor; unusual bodies are not automation.'),
 ('c0842','needs_evidence','automation','The Mech-Men reference establishes a mechanical-evolution theme but no applicable human support economy.','A genre-history citation is insufficient; no complete old magazine is recovered to rescue the lead.'),
 ('c0843','boundary_case','mechanistria','Mechanistria is a hostile machine ecology rather than a verified human-derived beneficiary society.','Organic visitors face dissection, not settled post-work provision.'),
 ('c0844','needs_evidence','automation','The Jonnemacher novel’s automation-dystopia label does not supply a verified living population’s material rules.','The specialist reference names the work, but its ordinary access and detailed chronology remain unresolved after the short check.')
]
D=[short_disposition(cid,status,why,[P+key],analysis) for cid,status,key,why,analysis in cases]
D += [decision(r['candidate_id'],'zero_variant' if r['record_type']=='zero_variant' else 'included','The scoped references identify implemented technological support or a direct preference for retained human work despite automation.',r['source_ids'],society_id=r['id']) for r in R]
D.sort(key=lambda x:x['candidate_id'])
write_batch(95,[f'c{i:04}' for i in range(833,845)],S,R,D,[
 'Twelve sequential reference checks yield three records, including a directly evidenced News from Nowhere zero variant.',
 'Mizora guarantees are scoped to admitted women/daughters; racial and eugenic exclusions are not hidden and no speculative punishment method is asserted.',
 'News from Nowhere Chapter XXVII explicitly establishes capacity for almost all necessary work and chosen handicraft. Enjoyable work remains useful.',
 'Dodd’s short workday is not a participation fraction. Manufactured food and domestic automation are actual mechanisms, while narrative satire is separated from provision.',
 'No complete old novel, magazine, primary PDF or elaborate format reconstruction was used to rescue weak leads.',
 'Real Mizoram enterprises, historical radio/music broadcasts and unrelated technical papers were discarded.'
])
